    <bpmn:process id="W_W4468" name="W4468. Post-Incident &amp; Post-Accident Drug Testing (links VS-24/VS-147)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Workplace accident/incident (employee or customer); near-miss of severity
Frequency: Per incident
Volume: Post-incident tests (~accident/near-miss rate × severity threshold)
Owner: HSE (VS-24) / Occupational Health (VS-83) / HR (VS-103)
Participants: HSE (VS-24), Occupational Health (VS-83), HR (VS-103), Store Ops (VS-07), Customer Safety (VS-147), Legal (VS-100), Vendor (W4460)
Source: workflow W4468 — Post-Incident &amp; Post-Accident Drug Testing (links VS-24/VS-147)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4468_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4468_Lane1" name="HSE">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4468_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4468_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4468_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4468_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4468_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4468_Start3" name="Workplace accident/incident (employee or customer); near-miss of severity">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4468_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4468_Task4" name="HSE/Supervisor trigger post-incident testing per the threshold (any…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: HSE/Supervisor trigger post-incident testing per the threshold (any injury/property-damage/near-miss of defined severity, esp. involving safety-sensitive roles/drivers), immediately after securing the scene &amp; care (VS-24/VS-147)
Responsible (R): HSE / Supervisor
Accountable (A): HSE Lead / CHRO
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4468_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4468_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4468_Task5" name="HSE/Occupational Health/Vendor arrange immediate collection (within the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: HSE/Occupational Health/Vendor arrange immediate collection (within the detection window), chain-of-custody (W4469), MRO (W4470), and manage the employee (removal from duty, medical care)
Responsible (R): HSE / Occupational Health / Vendor
Accountable (A): HSE Lead / Occupational Health Lead
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4468_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4468_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4468_Task6" name="HSE/HR/Legal use the result in the incident investigation (VS-24/W4402)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: HSE/HR/Legal use the result in the incident investigation (VS-24/W4402), disciplinary/case (W4471), and any regulatory/insurance notification (VS-26/VS-147 W4405), with confidentiality
Responsible (R): HSE / HR / Legal
Accountable (A): HSE Lead / VP Legal
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4468_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
