      <bpmn:userTask id="W4470_Task4" name="MRO review every positive/invalid result — interview the employee for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: MRO review every positive/invalid result — interview the employee for legitimate medical explanation (valid prescription), verify prescription/medication, and distinguish true-positive from legitimate-medical-use
Responsible (R): MRO / Occupational Health
Accountable (A): MRO / Occupational Health Lead
Duration: Per positive</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4470_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4470_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4470_Task5" name="MRO validate the chain-of-custody/evidence integrity (W4469), confirm via…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: MRO validate the chain-of-custody/evidence integrity (W4469), confirm via split-specimen re-test on employee request, and issue the verified result
Responsible (R): MRO / Lab
Accountable (A): MRO
Duration: Per result</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4470_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4470_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4470_Task6" name="MRO/Occupational Health return the verified result to HR (confidentially W4462)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: MRO/Occupational Health return the verified result to HR (confidentially W4462) for action (W4471), retain records (VS-88), and ensure due process (W4471)
Responsible (R): MRO / Occupational Health / HR
Accountable (A): Occupational Health Lead / CHRO
Duration: Per result</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4470_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
