    <bpmn:process id="W_W4471" name="W4471. Positive/Refusal Result Case Management &amp; Due Process" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Verified positive / refusal-to-test result (W4470)
Frequency: Per positive/refusal
Volume: Positive/refusal cases (deterrence-dependent)
Owner: HR (VS-103) / Labor Relations (VS-84) / Legal (VS-100)
Participants: HR (VS-103), Labor Relations (VS-84), Legal (VS-100), Occupational Health (VS-83), HSE (VS-24), Security (VS-23), CHRO
Source: workflow W4471 — Positive/Refusal Result Case Management &amp; Due Process</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4471_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4471_Lane1" name="HR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4471_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4471_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4471_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4471_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4471_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4471_Start3" name="Verified positive / refusal-to-test result (W4470)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4471_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4471_Task4" name="due process">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: HR/Labor Relations open the case, notify the employee (confidentially W4462), provide the result &amp; evidence, and afford due process (right to explain, split-specimen re-test W4470, counsel/union representation per CBA VS-84)
Responsible (R): HR / Labor Relations / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO / VP Legal
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4471_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4471_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4471_Task5" name="HR/Labor Relations/Legal determine the outcome per policy (W4457) &amp; due process…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: HR/Labor Relations/Legal determine the outcome per policy (W4457) &amp; due process — rehabilitation pathway (W4473) for first-time/non-safety-critical; disciplinary/suspension; or separation (W4472) for severe/safety-sensitive/refusal/recurrent
Responsible (R): HR / Labor Relations / Legal / CHRO
Accountable (A): CHRO / VP Legal
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4471_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4471_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4471_Task6" name="HR/Legal document the case (records VS-88), manage confidentiality, handle any…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: HR/Legal document the case (records VS-88), manage confidentiality, handle any labor challenge/NLRC (W4472), and feed learning to deterrence analytics (W4478)
Responsible (R): HR / Legal / Labor Relations
Accountable (A): CHRO / VP Legal
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4471_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4471_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4471_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4471_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-681 (ensure controlled execution — Drug Testing Operations, Results &amp; Case Management (PA-150.2).) | - CTL-681: case opened confidentially; due process afforded (explain/re-test/representation); outcome per policy &amp; consistent; documented; NLRC-ready
Owner: HR (VS-103) / Labor Relations (VS-84) / Legal (VS-100)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
